{"version" 2 "boxes" [{"id" "stacktrinket_long_memory_ecology" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "stacktrinket_renderer"} "name" "long memory ecology" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 1280.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_long_memory_ecology_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nLong memory ecology: the previous frame steers where it is read from next. Its own red\nand green, then blue and alpha, become offsets into itself; two slow waves add a drift;\nfbm warped by the old picture is mixed in; and `ema` stores the result as four\nmemories at rates from 0.006 to 0.09. `mirror` folds the total back into 0..1.\n\nThe fold is what decides the look. `dup average … + +` adds each pixel's average back\non top every frame, so its values keep climbing, and `mirror` folds them into grain\nthat never settles. Delete that line and the reads, which together take in about 1.65\ntimes the old picture, slowly fill the memories instead, into a pale moving fog.\n\nThe program is in the [[property stackSL]] tab.\n*/\nstackFeedback()\n"} "stackSL" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_long_memory_ecology_stackSL_.stacksl" "inline" "# Nearby reads move through previous RGBA; the result is stored as four slow memories.\nprev\ndup xy 0.012 * sample\nswap zw 0.009 * sample\n+ 0.5 *\np ]wr9 0.006 * 0.004c0.17 +\np ]wa7 0.006 * 0.004s0.11 +\nvec2 sample\n0.65 * +\nuv 5.0 * prev 0.4 * + 0.02t + fbm\ndup 0.23 + dup 0.37 + dup 0.61 + vec4\n0.08 * +\nprev\n0.006_0.09\nema\ndup average\n0.015pulse0.23d0.09\n+ +\nmirror\nsaturate\n"}}} {"id" "stacktrinket_four_memory_bands" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "stacktrinket_renderer"} "name" "four memory bands" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [640.0 920.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_four_memory_bands_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nFour memory bands: red, green, blue and alpha are four separate memories of one slowly\nmoving fbm field, each offset a little. `0.015_0.18` is a range vector,\nvec4(0.015, 0.07, 0.125, 0.18): as the `ema` rate it makes red the slowest memory and\nalpha the fastest, so the colours separate where the field moves.\n\nThe program is in the [[property stackSL]] tab.\n*/\nstackFeedback()\n"} "stackSL" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_four_memory_bands_stackSL_.stacksl" "inline" "# RGBA are independent memories; the alpha vector gives each channel a different rate.\nuv 4.0 * 0.06t + fbm\ndup 0.17 +\ndup 0.41 +\ndup 0.73 +\nvec4\nprev\n0.015_0.18\nema\nsaturate\n"}}} {"id" "stacktrinket_subroutine_cse" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "stacktrinket_renderer"} "name" "subroutine cse" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 920.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_subroutine_cse_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nDefinitions: `: ring-a … ;` names a piece of program, and using the name runs it.\nring-a and ring-b are two remembered rings; ring-a is called twice. The compiler\ninlines definitions and notices the repeat: in the lowered GLSL in the glsl panel,\nring-a is computed once and its value used twice. The average of the three goes back\ninto red, and the palette colours it.\n\nA definition must leave the stack as deep as it found it: each ring is called with\n`input` on top, so it starts with `drop` and ends with its one ring in its place.\n\nThe program is in the [[property stackSL]] tab.\n*/\nstackFeedback()\n"} "stackSL" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_subroutine_cse_stackSL_.stacksl" "inline" "# ring-a and ring-b are deliberately similar; ring-a is called twice.\n: ring-a\n  drop\n  0-> 0.982 *\n  p length 0.42 0.035 pulse 0.08 *\n  +\n;\n\n: ring-b\n  drop\n  0-> 0.982 *\n  p length 0.52 0.035 pulse 0.05 *\n  +\n;\n\ndrop\ninput ring-a\ninput ring-b\n+\ninput ring-a\n+ 0.333 *\ndup ->0\npalette\nsaturate\n"}}} {"id" "stacktrinket_store_channels" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "stacktrinket_renderer"} "name" "store channels" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [640.0 560.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_store_channels_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nStore channels. `0->` reads the red channel of this pixel's store, which here is the\nprevious frame, and `->0`, `->1`, `->2` write one value into red, green and blue. The\nring's brightness steps at random ten times a second (`|sh10`), and red keeps it as a\nslow memory; green and blue are fixed fractions of it, so the colour is a warm orange.\n\nThe program is in the [[property stackSL]] tab.\n*/\nstackFeedback()\n"} "stackSL" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_store_channels_stackSL_.stacksl" "inline" "# 0-> reads the red memory for this pixel; ->0 explicitly keeps it.\n0-> 0.985 *\np length 0.5 0.08 |sh10 pulse\n0.08 *\n+\ndup ->0\ndup 0.65 * ->1\ndup 0.35 * ->2\nsaturate\n"}}} {"id" "stacktrinket_pulse_ring" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "stacktrinket_renderer"} "name" "pulse ring" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 200.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_pulse_ring_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nStackSL is a stack language in which every value is a vec4. A program starts with\ninput = vec4(uv, hash, time) on the stack; each word takes values off the top and\npushes its result, and whatever is on top at the end is the colour of the pixel.\n\nThis box's program is in its [[property stackSL]] tab. `p` is uv centred on the\nmiddle, `length` its distance from there, `0.5 0.08 pulse` a soft band at radius 0.5,\nand `white *` colours it.\n\nstackFeedback() draws the program over the whole window every frame, with the frame\nbefore bound as `state`: `prev` reads it at this pixel, `0.004 0 vec2 sample` a little\nto the side. Edit the program while it runs and the new one takes over without\nclearing the picture; run this box again to start from black. The lowering panel\nshows how deep the stack ends (here 2: the input is still under the ring) and any\nerror at its line and column; open the glsl panel for the GLSL the program becomes.\n*/\nstackFeedback()\n"} "stackSL" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_pulse_ring_stackSL_.stacksl" "inline" "p\nlength\n0.5 0.08 pulse\nwhite *\n"}}} {"id" "stacktrinket_feedback_fog" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "stacktrinket_renderer"} "name" "feedback fog" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [640.0 200.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_feedback_fog_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nFeedback fog: each frame keeps 98.2% of the last one and adds a little moving fbm,\ncoloured by the cosine palette. A pixel settles where the decay and the addition\nbalance, about 0.08 / 0.018 = 4.4 times the palette colour, so most of it clips to\nbright. Try `prev 0.9 *` for a thinner fog that follows the noise more closely.\n\nThe program is in the [[property stackSL]] tab.\n*/\nstackFeedback()\n"} "stackSL" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_feedback_fog_stackSL_.stacksl" "inline" "prev 0.982 *\nuv 5.5 * 0.12t + fbm\npalette 0.08 *\n+\n"}}} {"id" "stacktrinket_renderer" "properties" {"children" #{#afield/box "stacktrinket_pulse_ring" #afield/box "stacktrinket_feedback_fog" #afield/box "stacktrinket_persistent_bloom" #afield/box "stacktrinket_store_channels" #afield/box "stacktrinket_subroutine_cse" #afield/box "stacktrinket_four_memory_bands" #afield/box "stacktrinket_long_memory_ecology"} "parents" #{#afield/box "root"} "name" "renderer" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 40.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_renderer_code_.kt" "inline" "import afield.graphics.vulkan.util.Options\n\nprop<Window>(window)\nprop<Renderer>(renderer)\nOptions.enableHDR = false\n// once: re-running this box keeps the existing window and renderer\nonce.renderer {\n    window = Window(\"StackTrinket\", initialDimensions = Rect(80.0, 80.0, 760.0, 760.0))\n    Renderer(window)\n}\n// the frame loop runs as this box's coroutine; stopping the box stops rendering\nstart(renderer::run)\n"}}} {"id" "stacktrinket_persistent_bloom" "properties" {"children" #{} "parents" #{#afield/box "root" #afield/box "stacktrinket_renderer"} "name" "persistent bloom" "_tombstone" false "frame" #afield/rect [40.0 560.0 300.0 100.0] "code" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_persistent_bloom_code_.kt" "inline" "/*\nPersistent bloom: a ring at radius 0.32 whose colour drifts round the palette\n(`0.08t palette`), added on top of 96.5% of the previous frame. The ring remembers\nevery colour it has been, so it slowly burns towards white.\n\nThe program is in the [[property stackSL]] tab.\n*/\nstackFeedback()\n"} "stackSL" #afield/file-inline {"path" "stacktrinket_persistent_bloom_stackSL_.stacksl" "inline" "prev 0.965 *\np length 0.32 0.05 pulse\n0.08t palette\n*\n+\n"}}}] "persistentProperties" ["frame" "name" "code" "code_language" "contents_language" "default_property" "file_proxy_mode" "file_proxy_path" "file_proxy_original_path" "file_proxy_mime" "filename" "preamble" "introduction" "attic" "notes" "geometryReviews" "geometryAppearance" "fragment" "stackSL" "rectSL" "msl" "vertex" "vertex_fragment" "task" "mesh" "raygen" "miss" "closesthit" "anyhit" "intersection" "callable" "fragment_s" "vertex_s" "task_s" "mesh_s" "raygen_s" "miss_s" "closesthit_s" "anyhit_s" "intersection_s" "callable_s" "children" "parents" "compute" "compute_s" "customization" "source_id" "templateId" "_tombstone" "isRemoteJSRoot" "isPythonRoot" ".*_editorState" "metadata" "nested" "nestedIn" "playlist" "pauseList" "bookmarks" "drawing" "panes" "slideShow" "autorun" "layers" "layerFrames" "_controlGroupValues" "keyframeData" "keyframeInterpolants" "ai4_auto_name" "ai4_auto_name_signature" "ai4_chat_history" "ai4_chat_running" "ai4_chat_suspension" "ai4_session" "fileManagerAccessHistory" "kitRole"]}